WEBVTT

00:02.520 --> 00:04.610
What're you looking at?

00:04.610 --> 00:06.490
A Herme's flyer.

00:06.490 --> 00:07.740
Oh.

00:07.740 --> 00:10.240
That one discount department store?

00:10.240 --> 00:10.990
That's right.

00:10.990 --> 00:12.990
There's a special sale starting today!

00:15.660 --> 00:18.250
Can you buy what you want there, Nene?

00:20.210 --> 00:22.880
World peace would probably be tricky.

00:22.880 --> 00:24.550
I'm not sure where they'd sell that.

00:26.670 --> 00:30.260
I've got too many witty responses to choose from.

00:30.260 --> 00:32.140
Is there anything you want, Clarin?

00:32.140 --> 00:34.680
Nothing at present.

00:35.010 --> 00:36.810
Is there anything you need, then?

00:39.480 --> 00:41.230
Equipment and reserves.

00:41.230 --> 00:43.150
All right! Let's go look for some.

00:44.190 --> 00:45.730
Come on, Clarin.

00:45.730 --> 00:50.320
I'm sure you know this by now,
but don't go anywhere dangerous.

00:54.580 --> 00:59.410
The very notion of a girl
is dangerous, simply by existence.

00:59.410 --> 01:00.960
'Tis a lethal weapon.

01:04.000 --> 01:05.210
BUER!

02:36.890 --> 02:40.060
The Herme's third
anniversary sale has begun!

02:40.060 --> 02:42.520
Bargain prices! Low as can be!

02:42.810 --> 02:46.810
Today's enormous sales event features the latest in disaster-preventing goods!

02:46.810 --> 02:50.360
In addition, we're kicking off the day with a balloon festival!

02:48.860 --> 02:51.650
Hurry, Mom! Hurry!

02:52.240 --> 02:53.400
Wait for me.

02:53.950 --> 02:56.450
Billy! No running, now!

02:56.450 --> 02:58.990
This place is amazing, Clarin.

02:59.780 --> 03:03.580
Want to start with the top floor?

03:03.580 --> 03:06.670
You might find something you want.

03:09.210 --> 03:10.880
I smell it. I smell it!

03:10.880 --> 03:13.630
The swirling greed of the vulgar masses.

03:13.630 --> 03:15.170
'Tis a lethal weapon!

03:17.930 --> 03:23.560
And now, I'd like to introduce the manager-for-the-day for today's sales event!

03:25.230 --> 03:28.690
The chairman of the Cenancle
Self-Governance Organization, Mister North!

03:30.520 --> 03:31.820
Ladies and gentlemen!

03:31.820 --> 03:34.650
I thank you for gathering here today!

03:34.650 --> 03:38.990
Indeed, I am this island's
government chairman, Janus North!

03:40.870 --> 03:44.750
Make no mistake, this local occasion is not your typical sales event.

03:44.750 --> 03:49.250
It's a countermeasure against the terrorism incident the other day in Vulcan,

03:49.250 --> 03:51.840
and the network outages that we've been plagued with recently.

03:53.460 --> 03:57.340
You'll of course find the typical supplies of food and drinking water today,

03:57.340 --> 04:00.340
but take notice of the fuel, generators,
and other such stock today!

04:02.260 --> 04:07.980
In the event of a disaster, Herme's will hand these goods out free of charge!

04:09.190 --> 04:13.480
I'm sincerely grateful to the Herme's department store

04:14.030 --> 04:18.910
for its considerable cooperation with these groundbreaking measures the CSGO and I devised!

04:20.070 --> 04:23.990
And now Mr. North, the mascot designed after Chairman North

04:23.990 --> 04:26.250
will present the chairman with a bouquet.

04:26.250 --> 04:27.870
Oh, Mr. North!

04:27.870 --> 04:28.580
Yay!

04:30.120 --> 04:32.170
I've been waiting for this day!

04:35.380 --> 04:36.130
What!?

04:36.420 --> 04:37.800
Chairman North!

04:37.800 --> 04:42.720
Controversy has arisen over your
extravagant private life, palatial residence,

04:42.720 --> 04:45.430
and recent purchase of a super deluxe custom limousine

04:45.430 --> 04:48.180
so large that it couldn't even fit in Herme's parking lot.

04:48.180 --> 04:49.730
Care to comment?

04:52.940 --> 04:54.400
Controversy!?

05:01.610 --> 05:06.290
Our sensible islanders wouldn't want some shabby-looking diplomat representing them!

05:06.620 --> 05:08.450
That's enough out of you, Mr. Chairman!

05:08.450 --> 05:09.540
How dare you.

05:09.540 --> 05:12.290
Wh-Who the hell are you!?

05:12.290 --> 05:14.460
If you want to know, I'll tell you!

05:14.460 --> 05:18.170
I'm the futuristic heart-throbbing
journalist who just got a scoop that will,

05:18.170 --> 05:19.090
or at least I hope will,

05:19.090 --> 05:21.180
carry me to stardom!

05:21.180 --> 05:22.430
My name is Vli—

05:26.060 --> 05:27.770
What's her deal?

05:33.190 --> 05:36.860
Clarin, why can't we take that pretty elevator over there?

05:36.860 --> 05:38.190
It lets you see outside.

05:38.610 --> 05:39.820
Dangerous.

05:39.820 --> 05:41.530
Do you have trouble with heights?

05:41.530 --> 05:42.450
Wrong.

05:43.160 --> 05:45.950
It's inadvisable from a security standpoint.

05:46.580 --> 05:48.950
I want to avoid the risk of snipers.

05:48.950 --> 05:52.460
Tempered glass is powerless against .50 caliber ammo.

05:52.790 --> 05:54.080
Huh...

05:55.880 --> 05:58.050
What was the meaning of that?

05:58.050 --> 06:00.510
Such disrespect, right in front of the press.

06:00.510 --> 06:01.880
I apologize, sir.

06:01.880 --> 06:04.590
A freelance journalist evidently slipped into the mix.

06:06.180 --> 06:07.510
Which floor?

06:07.510 --> 06:09.430
The floor where I can eat yakisoba.

06:09.430 --> 06:10.770
The 20th floor.

06:10.770 --> 06:11.480
Yes, ma'am.

06:13.560 --> 06:15.610
<i>A high-grade android?</i>

06:15.610 --> 06:16.730
<i>Two of them, even.</i>

06:17.230 --> 06:19.030
<i>These things are the reason the press</i>

06:19.030 --> 06:24.240
<i>always prattles on about jobs being taken and the recession we're in.</i>

06:25.820 --> 06:28.030
My fifth leg hath whispered to me!

06:28.030 --> 06:30.200
An ominous chaos creeps upon us!

06:30.950 --> 06:33.290
Uh, this is just, um...

06:33.290 --> 06:36.000
I feel it! It seethes!! It surgeth!

06:36.000 --> 06:37.880
'Tis a network outage!

06:47.220 --> 06:51.220
It's another network outage, ma'am.

06:51.220 --> 06:52.930
I don't give a damn...

06:52.930 --> 06:55.390
That's not even newsworthy anymore.

06:55.390 --> 06:59.570
But I bet it'd be awarded if I got the scoop on what's causing it.

06:59.570 --> 07:02.150
The data transmission stopped.

07:02.650 --> 07:03.900
What's going on!?

07:03.900 --> 07:05.240
Do something!

07:05.240 --> 07:06.570
As if I can...

07:07.530 --> 07:08.660
What the...

07:09.120 --> 07:11.080
There's a fire! A scoop!

07:11.080 --> 07:11.910
You're joking!

07:11.910 --> 07:12.660
You mean smoking!?

07:13.160 --> 07:15.540
Attention, all customers.

07:15.540 --> 07:20.960
A network outage is effecting the Mercury area.

07:20.960 --> 07:25.630
Do they have any idea how much economic loss these outages are causing?

07:25.630 --> 07:27.680
Mr. Chairman, let's return to CSGO headquarters.

07:27.680 --> 07:28.300
Agreed.

07:31.010 --> 07:32.470
We stopped.

07:33.430 --> 07:35.230
Great, just great!

07:35.230 --> 07:40.270
Where does this leave me, now that I've given this store preferential treatment for their contributions!?

07:40.270 --> 07:42.020
Mr. Chairman, I understand.

07:42.020 --> 07:45.610
But if you keep carrying on like this in front of others, I'll have to use the stungun.

07:46.450 --> 07:49.950
These robots might as well be vending machines during these network outages.

07:49.950 --> 07:51.410
There's no cause for concern.

07:51.410 --> 07:54.450
There are probably restrictions on their behaviors and recordings.

07:54.450 --> 07:56.040
Um...

07:56.580 --> 07:59.330
Then please show a bit more composure!

07:59.330 --> 08:03.130
If it's a network outage, it will be over in about 30 minutes.

08:03.130 --> 08:05.300
That's not good enough.

08:05.300 --> 08:06.420
Mr. Chairman?

08:07.090 --> 08:11.930
I've got an emergency situation to deal with.

08:13.310 --> 08:16.680
Is that emergency number one,
or emergency number two?

08:18.270 --> 08:19.690
Emergency...

08:19.690 --> 08:20.690
number <i>two</i>.

08:22.980 --> 08:25.070
Mayday! Mayday! Mayday!

08:25.070 --> 08:26.110
We have an emergency here!

08:26.110 --> 08:28.030
Security, respond!

08:33.870 --> 08:36.660
We're not getting through...

08:36.660 --> 08:37.830
Mr. Chairman! How long do we have?

08:38.160 --> 08:40.960
Ten. No, five...

08:42.290 --> 08:43.590
Mr. Chairman!

08:44.590 --> 08:46.050
Please use these.

08:46.880 --> 08:50.470
Fortunately, it's just me and the androids here.

08:50.470 --> 08:51.590
If worst comes to worst...

08:55.140 --> 08:57.770
Uh, about that...

08:58.850 --> 09:00.900
I'm human.

09:02.560 --> 09:04.650
Please excuse my rudeness, miss!

09:04.650 --> 09:07.400
I'm Janus North, chairman of this island's government.

09:07.400 --> 09:09.240
It's nice to meet you!

09:09.240 --> 09:10.820
I'm Nanakorobi Nene.

09:10.820 --> 09:12.110
Nice to meet you too.

09:12.910 --> 09:16.200
<i>Maintaining his public image is
only making this harder for him.</i>

09:17.370 --> 09:19.000
<i>Is he nearing his breaking point!?</i>

09:19.000 --> 09:20.160
Um...

09:22.880 --> 09:23.750
Mr. Chairman!

09:25.380 --> 09:27.050
Just breathe slowly...

09:28.670 --> 09:31.510
Please hold on, Mr. Chairman!

09:31.510 --> 09:32.550
Clarin.

09:34.800 --> 09:37.140
Pandora Device, open!

09:37.140 --> 09:39.020
Decode skill.

09:39.020 --> 09:42.440
Elpis Series, Healing Space!

09:49.690 --> 09:54.240
<i>My heart, my troubles, all being healed...</i>

09:55.490 --> 09:59.250
<i>My painful memories are fading away.</i>

09:59.660 --> 10:01.160
It's not helping!

10:01.160 --> 10:02.040
Mr. Chairman!

10:02.040 --> 10:03.500
Are you all right, Mr. Chairman!?

10:03.500 --> 10:07.210
Maybe it'll just be gas...

10:07.210 --> 10:07.920
Pardon?

10:07.920 --> 10:10.760
When I relax, it's actually not that bad...

10:11.800 --> 10:12.630
M-Mr. Chairman!

10:12.630 --> 10:14.090
Be patient, we'll be out soon!

10:14.090 --> 10:15.390
Please don't give up!

10:16.720 --> 10:17.640
Out?

10:21.350 --> 10:22.270
I opened it.

10:22.890 --> 10:24.310
Wow, Clarin!

10:24.810 --> 10:27.820
T-T-Toilet!

10:28.150 --> 10:29.280
Close call...

10:30.480 --> 10:32.740
Verily, now is a golden time!

10:32.740 --> 10:33.820
Oh!

10:37.490 --> 10:39.790
It's kind of dark in here.

10:39.790 --> 10:41.450
Oh, I could open this.

10:44.540 --> 10:45.710
That door is dangerous!

10:53.590 --> 10:55.470
You sure saved me.

10:55.470 --> 10:57.090
We really are grateful.

10:57.090 --> 10:58.930
Some day I'll repay—

10:58.930 --> 11:00.430
Um...

11:01.430 --> 11:04.980
No!

11:16.070 --> 11:17.240
Where's our backup!?

11:17.240 --> 11:18.120
I don't know!

11:18.120 --> 11:20.990
The chain of command's screwed up thanks to the network outage!

11:21.410 --> 11:24.040
The sprinklers and alarms didn't go off?

11:24.040 --> 11:25.330
What's going on here!?

11:25.330 --> 11:26.620
Behold!

11:25.330 --> 11:26.920
We have absolutely no idea.

11:26.920 --> 11:30.000
They say before anyone knew it, it was on fire!

11:26.920 --> 11:30.000
The Herme's department store is about to burn down!

11:30.000 --> 11:32.420
Panic fills the scene.

11:32.420 --> 11:35.260
Just what could have led to this!?

11:35.800 --> 11:38.760
The great soul power of the press!

11:35.800 --> 11:38.760
Could this be premeditated arson?

11:38.760 --> 11:39.680
I'm on fire here!

11:38.760 --> 11:41.260
You think it's terrorism!?

11:39.680 --> 11:41.260
Burn, baby! Burn!

11:41.260 --> 11:42.930
You there! What are you doing!?

11:42.930 --> 11:44.140
Shit!

11:44.430 --> 11:45.520
Hey, she ran off!

11:45.520 --> 11:46.390
That's suspicious!

11:46.690 --> 11:48.400
Get back here!

11:50.310 --> 11:52.190
Mr. Chairman, it's a dead end here!

11:52.730 --> 11:54.400
They've already finished evacuations!

11:54.820 --> 11:57.030
The alarm never even went off!

11:57.030 --> 11:58.660
Clarin, be careful!

12:09.540 --> 12:12.380
The stairs are still intact on the lower level.

12:13.630 --> 12:16.420
That does look like an escape route.

12:16.420 --> 12:19.390
Damn, if only I were twenty years younger...

12:19.390 --> 12:20.680
You'd be able to fly?

12:27.810 --> 12:30.850
Th-There shouldn't be anything creating poisonous gas!

12:32.480 --> 12:34.530
But this much smoke alone will still suffocate us!

12:34.900 --> 12:36.070
Here, use this.

12:39.320 --> 12:40.450
Thank you.

12:40.450 --> 12:41.820
Nene, you said, right?

12:42.450 --> 12:44.910
Did you see a rope ladder, or rope itself?

12:44.910 --> 12:46.250
You see anything?

12:46.250 --> 12:47.580
None detected.

12:47.580 --> 12:48.830
I see.

12:48.830 --> 12:51.130
Wait here, you two.

12:51.130 --> 12:52.170
Yes, sir.

12:52.170 --> 12:53.460
Oh, but...

12:53.880 --> 12:56.800
I'll go find a way down there.

12:56.800 --> 12:58.760
Mr. Chairman, I'll go with you.

12:59.880 --> 13:00.760
Nene.

13:01.300 --> 13:02.510
Thanks.

13:08.480 --> 13:10.980
There's no getting through this sales floor.

13:10.980 --> 13:14.230
It's over 300°C beyond the wall of fire.

13:14.230 --> 13:16.610
The lower floors are about 400°C on average.

13:16.610 --> 13:17.990
Continuing to rise.

13:17.990 --> 13:22.030
But Nene's and Clarion's durability will allow for quick passage.

13:22.740 --> 13:24.490
I recommend a prompt evacuation.

13:25.580 --> 13:26.910
Clarin, wait.

13:27.750 --> 13:29.830
Those other two are still inside.

13:29.830 --> 13:32.500
Their chances of survival are extremely low.

13:32.500 --> 13:34.000
That's not true!

13:34.000 --> 13:36.460
There's gotta be some way we can all escape!

13:40.970 --> 13:43.300
Yeah! That might work!

13:43.300 --> 13:44.890
Clarin, help me!

13:50.600 --> 13:53.060
Pandora Device, open!

13:54.020 --> 13:56.940
Decode skill, Elpis Series!

13:57.860 --> 13:59.190
Couturier!

14:05.070 --> 14:08.290
Chairman North, the fire's spread to the stairway.

14:08.290 --> 14:12.710
Shit! I can't afford to die now, in a place like this!

14:12.710 --> 14:15.580
I don't exactly want to die along with you, either...

14:17.630 --> 14:20.210
Damn it, isn't there a way down!?

14:28.680 --> 14:31.060
Sorry! Are you all right?

14:31.060 --> 14:32.730
What is this?

14:33.140 --> 14:35.230
Be careful you don't bite your tongue.

14:37.820 --> 14:39.940
Clarin, is the path clear?

14:39.940 --> 14:41.190
No problem.

14:41.190 --> 14:44.740
But all this audio noise is slowing down the visual processing.

14:44.740 --> 14:46.740
Okay, I'll do what I can!

14:47.450 --> 14:48.950
<i>Echolocation?</i>

14:48.950 --> 14:50.990
<i>You mean they're visualizing sound?</i>

14:51.290 --> 14:53.910
<i>But how? They don't have any equipment.</i>

14:55.370 --> 14:56.830
Our oxygen is...

14:56.830 --> 14:58.170
Please use these!

14:58.790 --> 15:00.750
But what about what your share?

15:01.170 --> 15:05.260
We'll be fine for a while,
with the oxygen stored inside us!

15:08.890 --> 15:10.430
We'll be there soon!

15:10.430 --> 15:15.020
<i>Come to think of it, there was a report
about an adepter moving to this island.</i>

15:15.020 --> 15:17.020
<i>Was it referring to these two?</i>

15:19.480 --> 15:20.440
Warning.

15:20.440 --> 15:21.900
Obstacle detected.

15:21.900 --> 15:23.110
Leave it to me!

15:23.110 --> 15:26.950
<i>Were they successful in becoming full-body cyborgs</i>

15:28.570 --> 15:30.530
<i>when there are still so few worldwide?</i>

15:34.750 --> 15:37.370
<i>But even if they are full-body cyborgs,</i>

15:37.790 --> 15:42.380
<i>can they really tread the line between man and machine this freely?</i>

15:38.670 --> 15:39.880
Please hurry!

15:47.760 --> 15:49.090
Amazing!

15:49.090 --> 15:51.760
We actually made it to the emergency stairs!

15:52.100 --> 15:55.140
Who on earth <i>are</i> you two?

15:56.600 --> 15:59.150
Nanakorobi Nene, and Clarin.

15:59.150 --> 16:00.020
Clarion.

16:00.610 --> 16:03.070
And cute, to boot...

16:17.870 --> 16:19.040
There's a child.

16:19.790 --> 16:22.380
I recommend a prompt evacuation.

16:22.380 --> 16:24.670
Clarin? But...

16:24.670 --> 16:26.090
he has to come with us.

16:26.090 --> 16:27.590
Temporal limit.

16:27.930 --> 16:31.720
But if we don't save him, he'll die here!

16:31.720 --> 16:35.180
Our actions are the outcome of optimal decisions.

16:35.180 --> 16:36.980
It's not your responsibility.

16:37.730 --> 16:38.600
Nene?

16:38.600 --> 16:40.730
Oh, s-sorry...

16:41.230 --> 16:43.270
But... But, you know...

16:43.270 --> 16:44.610
We all need to...

16:48.900 --> 16:51.240
Dad... Mom...

16:54.370 --> 16:59.120
The building's structural integrity won't last long in this fire.

16:59.580 --> 17:02.250
There is also the danger of combustible gas.

17:02.250 --> 17:03.670
We must evacuate immediately.

17:03.670 --> 17:05.420
You go on ahead, Clarin!

17:05.420 --> 17:07.920
I have to save that boy!

17:13.140 --> 17:15.100
Billy! Billy!

17:15.100 --> 17:17.980
Somebody, save my son!

17:17.980 --> 17:19.640
Survivors!

17:21.480 --> 17:23.440
Mr. Chairman! Thank goodness you're safe!

17:23.440 --> 17:25.940
A-All in a day's work.

17:25.940 --> 17:27.230
But never mind that.

17:27.230 --> 17:30.070
Where are those girls who escaped with us?

17:30.070 --> 17:32.660
They saved our lives.

17:32.660 --> 17:34.240
Are the two of them safe?

17:34.240 --> 17:37.540
You two came out of there alone!

17:37.540 --> 17:38.660
Say what!?

17:38.950 --> 17:42.330
What? But we all escaped together!

17:42.330 --> 17:44.080
How can this be?

17:44.080 --> 17:46.000
Nanakorobi Nene!

17:46.000 --> 17:47.170
Clarin!

17:48.920 --> 17:50.010
Nene?

17:56.430 --> 17:57.850
Hang on!

17:57.850 --> 17:59.930
You're going to be okay!

18:03.190 --> 18:04.690
We need to hurry!

18:08.320 --> 18:10.190
Everyone, please stand back!

18:10.190 --> 18:11.450
It's not safe this close!

18:20.870 --> 18:22.290
The stairway...

18:23.920 --> 18:25.460
The cylinder's running out!

18:30.090 --> 18:33.010
<i>I'll force out my internal oxygen.</i>

18:33.010 --> 18:34.630
<i>That'll buy some time.</i>

18:40.930 --> 18:42.230
It's all right.

18:42.230 --> 18:45.480
That was a good luck charm, so I'm sure we'll make it.

18:46.690 --> 18:48.110
<i>My oxygen reserves are low...</i>

18:49.190 --> 18:50.480
<i>But...</i>

18:50.900 --> 18:53.490
<i>I swear I won't give up!</i>

18:56.620 --> 19:01.240
<i>I have to survive... and apologize to Clarin...</i>

19:06.040 --> 19:08.590
I still haven't found the stuff I want.

19:13.340 --> 19:15.550
It's... Clarin...

19:17.260 --> 19:21.890
Clarin, your ear is burnt.

19:26.770 --> 19:28.020
Hey, look!

19:28.020 --> 19:29.230
Somebody's there!

19:39.240 --> 19:41.790
But I told you to go on ahead.

19:41.790 --> 19:44.120
Nene's life is the top priority.

19:44.120 --> 19:45.750
The child won't survive.

19:45.750 --> 19:46.540
Not good enough.

19:46.960 --> 19:48.540
Then what do you want to do?

19:48.540 --> 19:51.550
Me? I want to save him.

19:54.840 --> 19:57.090
Oh, no! At that speed...

19:58.800 --> 19:59.850
Clarin...

19:59.850 --> 20:02.180
We <i>all</i> have to make it out!

20:02.180 --> 20:03.600
Agreed.

20:11.940 --> 20:13.610
What is this!?

20:13.610 --> 20:15.070
Give him to the rescuers.

20:15.070 --> 20:16.490
Make sure he survives.

20:17.030 --> 20:18.360
Oh, thank you.

20:19.280 --> 20:19.990
Who was that!?

20:20.870 --> 20:21.950
Over here!

20:21.950 --> 20:24.740
A child and woman, in need of medical attention!

20:24.740 --> 20:26.250
What? Me?

20:27.370 --> 20:28.500
Billy!

20:29.000 --> 20:30.250
Mama!

20:30.250 --> 20:32.420
He'll be okay, ma'am.

20:32.420 --> 20:34.880
Oh, Billy, thank God!

20:35.340 --> 20:38.260
Thank you! Thank you!

20:38.260 --> 20:39.260
Oh, thank God!

20:39.260 --> 20:41.390
You're a savior!

20:39.760 --> 20:41.390
Ma'am!

20:41.390 --> 20:43.390
You did it!

20:43.390 --> 20:44.140
What?

20:49.060 --> 20:50.600
Nene...

20:50.600 --> 20:51.860
Clarin...

20:51.860 --> 20:54.190
They saved us instead of...

20:54.190 --> 20:57.030
Mr. Chairman, those two are safe.

21:05.790 --> 21:08.040
Clarin? Are you okay?

21:08.040 --> 21:09.160
No problems.

21:09.160 --> 21:10.170
The child is also safe.

21:10.870 --> 21:13.170
Sorry, Clarin.

21:13.630 --> 21:15.920
Clarion should be the one to apologize.

21:16.630 --> 21:18.420
Nene made the right decision.

21:19.050 --> 21:24.470
Next time, we'll go buy something you want.

21:25.350 --> 21:26.430
It's a promise.

21:30.850 --> 21:33.440
Thou wilt go no farther on that leg.

21:33.810 --> 21:36.690
'Twould be wise to stop, and seek aid.

21:37.190 --> 21:38.320
Refusal.

21:38.320 --> 21:40.070
Nene's medical treatment is the top priority.

21:48.080 --> 21:48.830
Sheesh.

21:49.330 --> 21:52.830
I guess my warning not to go
anywhere dangerous didn't help.

22:04.260 --> 22:05.220
Colonel Kurtz!

22:05.220 --> 22:06.600
BUER has stabilized!

22:07.930 --> 22:10.100
So this is the result of a single sneeze.

22:15.270 --> 22:18.360
We'll make certain the CDF doesn't find out about this.

22:41.010 --> 22:44.010
Accessing the device named nature

22:44.010 --> 22:47.010
The circuit of infinite synapses

22:47.010 --> 22:47.550
read

22:47.550 --> 22:48.100
write

22:48.100 --> 22:48.760
enter

22:48.760 --> 22:49.390
code

22:49.390 --> 22:52.770
Sharing tools can lead to unavoidable situations

22:52.890 --> 22:55.150
Hey, Clarin, what kind of
equipment did you want anyway?

22:53.480 --> 23:04.070
{talk}{this is pandoradio, it'll change each week, ignore this segemnt}

22:55.150 --> 22:58.440
I could use some knives, guns, smoke screens, and electromagnetic capture nets.

22:58.440 --> 23:00.030
Old-school equipment, eh?

23:00.030 --> 23:01.440
Why not a Beam Rifle?

23:01.440 --> 23:02.690
Or a Lightsaber?

23:02.690 --> 23:04.070
I'll try asking Korobase for those.

23:04.070 --> 23:05.450
Saving data

23:05.450 --> 23:06.820
Strengthening predictions

23:06.820 --> 23:09.830
Even my latest updates

23:09.830 --> 23:15.120
can't help explain why you're so nice to me

23:15.120 --> 23:16.710
Error error

23:16.710 --> 23:18.210
parameter

23:18.210 --> 23:21.590
Please help me understand

23:21.590 --> 23:23.760
where these emotions came from.

23:23.760 --> 23:26.930
Find me at the end of this labrynth

23:26.930 --> 23:29.680
of feelings I can no longer control

23:29.680 --> 23:31.680
I understand the concept of emotions

23:31.680 --> 23:35.060
but I can't make any sense of my own

23:35.440 --> 23:38.060
I want to pull out these cords

23:38.400 --> 23:40.820
and head straight to you

23:40.820 --> 23:43.230
I won't come to understand love

23:43.230 --> 23:46.990
without having you here with me

23:52.620 --> 23:54.370
Whoa! My limousine!

23:54.370 --> 23:55.500
It's been crushed.

23:55.500 --> 23:57.040
Who did this!?

23:57.040 --> 24:00.040
Hey, press corps! One question at a time, here.

24:00.040 --> 24:03.170
I'm the star reporter of hope, Vli—

24:03.170 --> 24:04.090
Perhaps she did it?

24:04.090 --> 24:05.420
Cuff her!
